From: Paper Linux contributors <paperlinux@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] clk: imx35: expose the CLKO gate

The i.MX35 clock driver does not register the CCM CLKO output.  Boards such
as the Amazon Kindle 3 feed a 24 MHz CLKO into an external WM8960 audio
codec, so a codec consumer currently has no clock it can request or enable.

Select CKIH with a divide-by-one setting, matching the initialization in
the NXP/Lab126 2.6.26 clock code, then expose the existing CLKOEN bit as a
normal clock gate.  The output remains disabled unless a consumer requests
it.

Signed-off-by: Paper Linux contributors <paperlinux@localhost>
---
 drivers/clk/imx/clk-imx35.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/clk/imx/clk-imx35.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/imx/clk-imx35.c
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ enum mx35_clks {
 	/* 65 */ sdma_gate, spba_gate, spdif_gate, ssi1_gate, ssi2_gate,
 	/* 70 */ uart1_gate, uart2_gate, uart3_gate, usbotg_gate, wdog_gate,
 	/* 75 */ max_gate, admux_gate, csi_gate, csi_div, csi_sel, iim_gate,
-	/* 81 */ gpu2d_gate, ckil, clk_max
+	/* 81 */ gpu2d_gate, ckil, clko, clk_max
 };
 
 static struct clk *clk[clk_max];
@@ -105,6 +105,14 @@ static void __init _mx35_clocks_init(void)
 
 	clk[ckih] = imx_clk_fixed("ckih", 24000000);
 	clk[ckil] = imx_clk_fixed("ckil", 32768);
+	/*
+	 * CLKO's reset configuration is not represented by the common clock
+	 * framework.  Select the 24 MHz high-frequency crystal and divide it
+	 * by one before registering the output gate.
+	 */
+	__raw_writel((__raw_readl(base + 0x28) & ~0xfc5f) | 0x1,
+		     base + 0x28);
+	clk[clko] = imx_clk_gate("clko", "ckih", base + 0x28, 5);
 	clk[mpll] = imx_clk_pllv1(IMX_PLLV1_IMX35, "mpll", "ckih", base + MX35_CCM_MPCTL);
 	clk[ppll] = imx_clk_pllv1(IMX_PLLV1_IMX35, "ppll", "ckih", base + MX35_CCM_PPCTL);
 
-- 
